      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-6",
        "notes": "Read full Statement and Proof 1.1\u20133.1 and all ten declared suppliers. Explicit full/deleted sample-test product measurability now supplies Fubini; boundedness on probability products ensures L1. Swapping i and fresh coordinate preserves rectangle masses and hence product law. Common deletion gives replacement bound 2 beta_m, integrated deletion gives beta_m, and independence of held-out coordinate yields LOO identity. m=1 includes empty retained set; M=0 and beta_m=0 have no undefined subtraction. No AC, diagonal measurability shortcut, or monotonicity inference is needed. Reader real-Borel/product-space interface retained. Direct consumer high-probability theorem Statement and A2 already impose exactly these joint hypotheses; no consumer source repair."
