        "notes": "Read full Statement/Proof 1.1\u20133.1 and all nine suppliers, including amended expected theorem and complete McDiarmid proof. Common indexed deletion bounds full replacement by 2 beta_m. For j unequal k, a size-m sample with m-2 common observations and both alternatives has the two compared deleted samples up to simultaneous relabeling; permutation invariance yields 2 beta_m at the unchanged test point, without using beta_(m-1). k term is bounded by M. Thus both gaps oscillate by at most 4 beta_m+M/m. With c>0, t=c sqrt(m log(1/delta)/2) gives exponent log(delta); means are 2 beta_m and beta_m. c=0 forces M=beta_m=0; m=1 has no other indices; delta endpoints excluded. Full/deleted joint measurability meets repaired supplier. AC carried solely through McDiarmid. Separate probability events preserved. Reader interface clarification retained. Corrected full-proof locator to pp.507\u2013509; source comparison is evidence, not reliance on the paper\u2019s beta_(m-1) <= beta_m line."
